@startuml Communication-ProcessSale
' ===========================================================================
' POS System - Communication Diagram: Process Sale use case realization
' Software Engineering Practice - Part 2, artifact 4 (interaction diagrams)
'
' Shows the same interaction as the sequence diagram but in graph form, which
' is the space-economical form recommended for wall sketching.
' ===========================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam nodesep 34
skinparam ranksep 44
skinparam object {
  BackgroundColor #EAF2FB
  BorderColor #1F4E79
  ArrowColor #1F4E79
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #D6B656
}

' the actor, drawn as an object-shaped box so the messages read cleanly
object ":Cashier" as Cashier

object ":Register" as Register
object "s : Sale" as Sale
object "li : SalesLineItem" as LI
object "c : ProductCatalog" as Catalog
object "spec : ProductSpecification" as Spec
object "i : InventoryService" as Inv
object "p : Payment" as Payment
object "f : PaymentFactory" as Factory

' ---- makeNewSale ----------------------------------------------------------
Cashier --> Register : 1: makeNewSale()
Register --> Sale : 1.1: «create»

' ---- enterItem ------------------------------------------------------------
Cashier --> Register : 2: enterItem(itemID, qty)
Register --> Catalog : 2.1: getSpecification(itemID)
Catalog --> Spec : 2.1.1: [found]
Register --> LI : 2.2: «create»(spec, qty)
Register --> Sale : 2.3: makeLineItem(spec, qty)
Sale --> LI : 2.3.1: add(self)  ' GRASP Creator: Sale aggregates its line items
Register --> Inv : 2.4: isAvailable(itemID, qty)

' ---- getTotal -------------------------------------------------------------
Cashier --> Register : 3: getTotal()
Register --> Sale : 3.1: getTotal()
Sale --> LI : 3.1.1: getSubtotal()   ' loop for each line item
LI --> Spec : 3.1.1.1: [price]

' ---- makePayment ----------------------------------------------------------
Cashier --> Register : 4: makePayment(kind)
Register --> Factory : 4.1: create(kind, amount)
Factory --> Payment : 4.1.1: «create»
Register --> Sale : 4.2: makePayment(p)
Sale --> Payment : 4.2.1: authorize()
Register --> Inv : 4.3: remove(itemID, qty)   ' loop for each line item

' ---- endSale --------------------------------------------------------------
Cashier --> Register : 5: endSale()
Register --> Sale : 5.1: getChange()
Register --> Cashier : 5.2: receipt

note bottom of Register
  **GRASP decisions visible here**
  -- *Controller*: :Register is the facade controller, the first object
     beyond the UI layer to receive each system operation.
  -- *Creator*: :Register creates :Sale (1.1) and :Sale creates
     :SalesLineItem (2.2/2.3.1), because each records/aggregates the next.
  -- *Information Expert*: :Sale.getTotal (3.1) and
     :SalesLineItem.getSubtotal (3.1.1) are placed where the data is.
  -- *Factory*: :PaymentFactory owns payment creation (4.1), keeping
     that responsibility out of the domain.
  -- *Low Coupling*: :Register talks to :ProductCatalog through one
     lookup message and never reaches into a specification's internals.
end note

@enduml
